From: PS5_Proton <local@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: preserve PS5 mapping bounds when retrying native views

After an image allocation fails, clearing native-view metadata cannot extend
Sony's measured address aperture. Retry within the same clipped bounds and
with the same host-page-rounded length. An asset-free probe reproduces the
assertion when loading uxtheme after large placeholder reservations; pinned
Linux Wine completes the same contract. Keep other platforms unchanged.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -3007,7 +3007,13 @@
 
             clear_native_views();
             if (!is_win64) increase_try_map_step = FALSE;
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+            /* Native views are only metadata. Removing them does not extend
+             * the measured host aperture or change its page granularity. */
+            ptr = alloc_free_area( start, end, host_size, top_down, unix_prot, align_mask );
+#else
             ptr = alloc_free_area( (void *)limit_low, (void *)limit_high, size, top_down, unix_prot, align_mask );
+#endif
             if (!is_win64) increase_try_map_step = TRUE;
             if (!ptr) return STATUS_NO_MEMORY;
         }
